From b1335bd77ebcb9b7a3fcf28bb1d6761f4c10f4d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:26:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): dual contouring for the machined-stock mesh

Extract the stock field's surface by dual contouring (Ju, Losasso,
Schaefer & Warren, SIGGRAPH 2002) by default: one clamped QEF vertex per
sign-changing cell, Hermite normals read from the crossing sheet, and
ridge-biased corner crossings replaced by the trusted planes around them.
A pocket's floor/wall edge now survives (slot edge gap 0.0000 cells vs
0.36 with marching tetrahedra; box volume 480.000 vs 472.3). Marching
tetrahedra stays as IsoMethod::Marching and as the logged fallback for
any dual mesh that is not closed.

Fixes #23

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
